WEBVTT

00:00:05.719 --> 00:00:09.220
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Thursday the twenty-sixth. Can you all hear me?</v>

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.820
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, although someone's coming through twice.</v>

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.280
<v Priya Raman>That's me, sorry. Laptop and headset. There, better?</v>

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:21.000
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Jamie Brennan's absent today, so it's just us.</v>

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:27.170
<v Marcus Hale>Before we get serious, there's a birthday cake in the office. Quite a substantial one.</v>

00:00:27.679 --> 00:00:32.229
<v David Whitfield>Substantial as in enough for everyone, or you've already had a substantial bit?</v>

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:36.810
<v Marcus Hale>I'm giving you useful information, David. Don't interrogate the source.</v>

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:40.429
<v Hannah Price>He's definitely had some.</v>

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:43.299
<v Tomasz Nowak>You can hear the guilt through Teams.</v>

00:00:45.469 --> 00:00:48.270
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, excellent technical start. Let's have the updates.</v>

00:00:49.229 --> 00:00:50.979
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, I've got a few.</v>

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:54.820
<v Tomasz Nowak>The monthly fire alarm test, that's all done.</v>

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:57.619
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Tommo.</v>

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:04.189
<v Sarah Okafor>And I tested the fire alarm panel yesterday. It's all fine now.</v>

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:05.739
<v Priya Raman>Good, that's reassuring.</v>

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:12.760
<v Tomasz Nowak>The risk assessment for work on the Atlas is updated as well. All fine.</v>

00:01:15.109 --> 00:01:16.310
<v Hannah Price>Lovely, thanks.</v>

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:23.319
<v Tomasz Nowak>And the seals on the little water valve on two — replaced, that's sorted.</v>

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:26.430
<v David Whitfield>Nice one.</v>

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:34.459
<v Tomasz Nowak>My leak inspection on the Main Water Isolation Valve has moved. That's now due on the 3rd.</v>

00:01:36.099 --> 00:01:37.299
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, thanks, Tom.</v>

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:44.140
<v Marcus Hale>Mine's less cheerful. I can't get any further with the pre-use checks; can't get hold of the supplier.</v>

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.519
<v Callum Reid>Ah, right. That's frustrating.</v>

00:01:48.989 --> 00:01:56.340
<v Sarah Okafor>One cancellation as well: the filter swap on the tower isn't going ahead now. It's been rolled into next month's shutdown.</v>

00:01:58.180 --> 00:01:59.379
<v David Whitfield>Understood.</v>

00:02:01.439 --> 00:02:10.189
<v Marcus Hale>Oh, and just an observation: I saw the pressure on the line 3 barrel dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own.</v>

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:14.020
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, just something you noticed?</v>

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:17.360
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, that's all it was.</v>

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:20.349
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. What's new from production, Callum?</v>

00:02:21.719 --> 00:02:27.669
<v Callum Reid>We've got a jam on the spinner. It needs clearing and the sensors need checking. It's urgent.</v>

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:33.800
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, did you say clear it or check the sensors? You broke up halfway through.</v>

00:02:36.219 --> 00:02:40.419
<v Callum Reid>Both — clear the jam and check the sensors on the spinner.</v>

00:02:41.159 --> 00:02:43.610
<v David Whitfield>Right, so not just a mechanical clear-out.</v>

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:45.699
<v Callum Reid>Exactly, yeah.</v>

00:02:46.759 --> 00:02:48.509
<v Sarah Okafor>Can anyone take that on?</v>

00:02:50.139 --> 00:02:53.289
<v Tomasz Nowak>I can't take it, sorry. Haven't got the capacity.</v>

00:02:53.729 --> 00:02:55.479
<v Priya Raman>Neither can I, I'm afraid.</v>

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:59.449
<v Sarah Okafor>Right... no taker for that at the moment, then.</v>

00:03:00.189 --> 00:03:05.789
<v Sarah Okafor>David, can you schedule downtime for the Atlas with production at half two? That's low priority.</v>

00:03:06.099 --> 00:03:11.000
<v David Whitfield>Sorry, Sarah, I can't fit that in today. It'll need to be someone else.</v>

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:19.620
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Haley, can you take that instead — schedule downtime for the Atlas with production at half two? Still low priority.</v>

00:03:21.199 --> 00:03:26.449
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll schedule downtime for the Atlas with production at half two. Low priority, understood.</v>

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:33.919
<v Callum Reid>Sorry, just so I've heard that properly — that's arranging the downtime with production, not starting work on it?</v>

00:03:35.189 --> 00:03:36.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, just scheduling the downtime.</v>

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:42.680
<v Callum Reid>Right, got you. I was talking over the first bit.</v>

00:03:44.969 --> 00:03:47.069
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, we're on the same page.</v>

00:03:47.949 --> 00:03:49.699
<v Sarah Okafor>Anything else for this morning?</v>

00:03:50.409 --> 00:03:52.159
<v Hannah Price>Nothing from quality to add.</v>

00:03:52.939 --> 00:03:54.689
<v Priya Raman>No, nothing else from me.</v>

00:03:55.199 --> 00:03:56.949
<v Tomasz Nowak>That's my lot as well.</v>

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:04.439
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. The spinner is urgent, but we haven't got anyone taking the jam clearance and sensor checks.</v>

00:04:04.889 --> 00:04:08.039
<v Callum Reid>Yeah. Not the answer I'd hoped for, but understood.</v>

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:14.680
<v Marcus Hale>On a slightly brighter note, the cake has proper icing. None of that dry sponge business.</v>

00:04:15.919 --> 00:04:20.120
<v Hannah Price>That's a very detailed report for someone who hasn't admitted eating it.</v>

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:21.930
<v Marcus Hale>No comment.</v>

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:25.779
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, on that very convincing note — thanks, everyone.</v>
